WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:04.109
Beth: Alongside the more common conditions
which co-occur with Autism, there are

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:09.119
other classic medical conditions such
as epilepsy, gastrointestinal and

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.239
feeding issues or sleep disorders.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:15.789
Joe: Resolving sleep or gastrointestinal
problems may also offer behavioural

00:00:15.799 --> 00:00:19.550
benefits, as the quantity and
quality of sleep can affect the

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.800
severity of repetitive behaviours.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.320
Half of children with Autism have
trouble falling or staying asleep and

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.950
this could make their Autism worse.

00:00:28.219 --> 00:00:32.409
Beth: Researchers recognise that sleep is
needed for brain development and improved

00:00:32.409 --> 00:00:37.350
health, it improves mood, behaviour
and our mental state and therefore the

00:00:37.359 --> 00:00:39.440
lack of it is likely to have impact.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.070
Epilepsy can also be a problem.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:47.149
Symptoms include shaking, having seizures,
and staring blankly into space are

00:00:47.889 --> 00:00:49.999
closely linked to Autism characteristics.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:54.639
Joe: Also genetic conditions, such as
fragile X syndrome and tuberous sclerosis

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:57.050
complex are closely linked to Autism.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:02.540
One of the symptoms of Fragile X syndrome
is mild to severe intellectual disability

00:01:02.849 --> 00:01:06.830
and individuals with the syndrome,
display a wide variety of Autism features.

00:01:07.509 --> 00:01:11.190
Other neurological symptoms include
developmental delay and seizures.

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:15.860
Beth: It has been found that many children
with Tuberous sclerosis will be diagnosed

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:20.420
with Autism spectrum disorder and there
is a clear link with cognitive impairment.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:25.899
Whichever condition an individual has,
alongside their Autism spectrum disorder,

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.600
the conditions often seem inter-related.

00:01:29.139 --> 00:01:32.530
Joe: Some seem to be have a negative
impact such as sleep issues.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.840
Some can mask their main disorder
such as ADHD, but they have to be

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.320
looked at individually alongside
each other to assess their impact

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.859
on each other and subsequently the
individuals health and well-being.

